.TH "libnvmf_context_set_config" 9 "libnvmf_context_set_config" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_context_set_config \- Set the configuration for discovery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "void" libnvmf_context_set_config
.BI "(struct libnvmf_context *fctx "  ","
.BI "const struct libnvmf_config *config "  ","
.BI "const struct libnvmf_config_conn *conn "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "fctx" 12
Fabrics context of a discovery controller
.IP "config" 12
Resolved configuration, or NULL
.IP "conn" 12
Connection of the discovery controller in \fIconfig\fP
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBlibnvmf_discover\fP connects to the controllers in the discovery log
page. With a configuration, a controller gets the KX-HMAC-CHAP secrets
of the [Subsystem] or [Discovery Controller] section with its NQN. The
section must be in the same file as \fIconn\fP.

If no section sets the host secret, the controller uses the host secret
of the discovery controller. This is also what happens without a
configuration. The controller secret comes only from a section.

The caller keeps ownership of \fIconfig\fP and \fIconn\fP. They must stay valid
until \fBlibnvmf_discover\fP returns.
